.26% fund + £2.58 per month admin. Evidence from P12 shows new solution investments: CT Universal MAP Balanced 50%, HSBC Global Strategy Balanced 50%, both Risk level 5. P6 shows performance comparison: Zurich Managed AP 46.14%, Aviva Risk 5 portfolio 42.40%, IA Mixed 25.66%, Aviva My Future Focus 15.85%. P19 shows Zurich all-plans comparison: existing £127k vs new £115k mid-growth, effect -£12,000 or -9.4% decrease. P38 justifies Zurich switch citing no Risk 5 funds available, requiring blend of Risk 7 + Risk 2.","discrepancies":["Report asserts Aviva My Future Focus RiskAlignment comparison: existing 'Risk level 2 - Global Investments (up to 85% shares)' vs recommended 'Risk level 5'. Evidence P18 shows Aviva My Future Focus is 'Lifestage Investment Approach' (auto-switching), not static Risk 2; P6 labels it '15.85%' performance, not a risk level. Contradiction in how existing risk level is characterized.","Report states Zurich Charges '0.18% fund + £2.12 per month admin charge (0.93% total)' but derived figures show: £2.12/month = £25.44/year on £103,439.24 = 0.0246%, not enough to reach 0.93%. The 0.93% figure is computed from £961.98 annual charge / £103,438.71, implying the entire 0.93% is attributed to Zurich when it includes both Zurich and another arrangement's charges combined (per figure annotations, row computed on wrong plan).","Report projects Zurich switch effect at mid-growth of -£12,000 or -9.4% decrease (P19), but assesses Zurich switch as 'Better' on charges. Switching from 0.3% reduction in yield (existing) to 0.6% reduction in yield (new) contradicts the 'Better' assessment when the new solution underperforms.","Report asserts Zurich FundRange 60+ vs 80+, 'Better', but evidence does not provide Zurich fund count; P1 shows Zurich in comparison table but does not specify fund availability number. No corroborating passage for the 60+ assertion.","Report statement 'The plan itself is 0.06% more expensive than the recommended solution' (on Aviva My F