{"groupId":"G10.4","requirement":"Vulnerability has a material impact on the recommendation (overlay) — Limb: Appropriateness. The suitability report must fully support any assertions about client vulnerabilities, support needs, communication preferences, capacity and comprehension with evidence from the case file. Where vulnerabilities are identified, the recommendation must account for them materially.","reportSays":"The report identifies six specific foreseeable harms: (1) market volatility and fund fluctuations, mitigated by adviser monitoring and multi-asset funds; (2) underperformance of new funds versus existing, mitigated by critical yield analysis; (3) pension switching costs reducing fund value, mitigated by no exit penalties identified and charge comparison; (4) illiquidity and administration delays, mitigated by liquid cash reserves of £6,000 and 10-15 working day access timeframe; (5) loss of employer contributions if People's Pension is left, mitigated by retaining that scheme; and (6) Inheritance Tax impact from April 2027, mitigated by IHT analysis and monitoring. The report states the client has 'limited experience' but 'understand[s] that returns are not guaranteed' and that 'any potential underperformance would not have a detrimental impact on day-to-day living.' Risk rating was upgraded from 4 (questionnaire) to 5 (Balanced) on adviser assessment and client agreement. The model shows `/vulnerability/perClient[]/impactOnRecommendation[]` is absent — this path was not extracted, meaning the report does not explicitly state how identified vulnerabilities materially shaped the recommendation itself.","fileSays":"The Risk Profile [P1] shows the client answered 'No understanding/knowledge' to three knowledge questions: stocks and shares, EIS/VCTs, and pension planning and retirement income. The client has no investment experience in unit trusts, stocks, EIS/VCTs or pensions (all answered 'No' to 5-year history). The client does check valuations annually by themselves. Capacity for Loss questionnaire responses are recorded [P1] but the specific notes state 'No additional notes were recorded' [P2]. The agreed risk level is 5 Balanced [P3], justified by the fact-find showing the client 'Wants to consolidate to help him get his head around what he has' [P6]. The suitability report [P14] confirms the client was initially rated 4 (Cautious Balanced) by questionnaire but the adviser felt this 'didn't fully reflect your risk appetite' and 'We agreed that you are a risk rating 5 rather than a 4.' Page 4 also states 'You confirmed that you wish to increase your Risk rating to 5.' The report [P14] notes the client is 'in receipt of a full State Pension of approximately £230 per week, continue to work as an HGV driver earning around £300 per week net' with 'additional £20 per week from your role with the Sea Cadets' and partner Kim contributes £1,100 per month. A fact-find [P7] shows current monthly net income of £1,430 against expenditure of £1,718, creating a monthly deficit of £288. The cashflow model [P4] shows state pension will 'cover your bills in retirement' allowing the pension 'to keep growing for large ad hoc spends.' File notes [P22] record 'Zurich current risk – 7' and alternative options for other arrangements. The report [P20] recommends Power of Attorney be set up: 'It would also be prudent to set up and register Power of Attorney for your financial affairs / health and welfare, to ensure that in the event of your incapacity, your spouse or relative could act on your behalf.' There is no record in the case that the client has done this or that it was executed. No formal vulnerability assessment document exists. No health, mental capacity, or capability assessment appears in the file. No communication support adjustments are recorded. No third-party authority is documented as in force.","discrepancies":["Report asserts client has 'limited experience' but file shows 'No understanding/knowledge' on three specific investment knowledge areas (stocks/shares, EIS/VCTs, pension planning); this is a material difference in degree, not merely 'limited' but zero recorded knowledge in core domains","Report states client will 'continue to work as an HGV driver earning around £300 per week net' but Fact Find [P7] shows employment as 'CDH Recruitment' at £1,200 per month basic income, creating ambiguity about actual employment status and income stability","Report upgrades risk rating from 4 to 5 based on adviser assessment that questionnaire 'didn't fully reflect your risk appetite,' but client has zero understanding of pension planning and retirement income and no investment experience; the justification for upgrade to Balanced (risk 5) when knowledge is absent is not explained","Report identifies six foreseeable harms but does not state whether or how each harm materially affects the suitability of the recommendation to a client with zero pension knowledge and no investment experience","Report recommends 'prudent' setup of Power of Attorney [P20] but file contains no evidence this was completed, executed or registered; no third-party authority or trusted contact is documented as in force","Report does not explicitly address whether the client's current monthly deficit of £288 [P7/P12] and reliance on pension drawdown in early retirement affects suitability of the risk rating or recommendation","Report states client 'are not reliant upon your pension funds' [P14] but Fact Find shows client needs £1,700 net monthly in retirement and will be drawing from pension to meet shortfall; this contradicts the assertion of non-reliance","Fact Find [P6] records consolidation as the client's own objective ('Wants to consolidate to help him get his head around what he has') but this is not framed as a vulnerability or support need in the report's vulnerability section; it may indicate cognitive or comprehension challenge not explicitly assessed"],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":["No formal vulnerability assessment document in the file","No mental capacity or capability assessment","No health or wellbeing assessment","No communication support or accessible format requirement (Fact Find [P29] shows 'No Requirement')","No evidence that recommended Power of Attorney was executed or is in force","No explicit statement of how each identified foreseeable harm materially shaped the recommendation for this specific client","No assessment of impact of current monthly cash flow deficit on suitability of risk rating","Extracted model path `/vulnerability/perClient[]/impactOnRecommendation[]` is absent from canonical model — report does not state material impact link"],"analysis":"The check requires evidence that vulnerability information in the report is 'fully supported' and that 'material clarification or additional evidence' is not needed. Several gaps emerge. First, the client's knowledge level: the Risk Profile [P1] documents zero understanding of three core investment domains (stocks, EIS/VCTs, pension planning), yet the report characterises this as 'limited experience' [P14] and upgrades risk from 4 to 5. The file shows no assessment of why zero pension knowledge supports a Balanced (higher-risk) rating, nor any evidence the client comprehends what 'Balanced' entails. Second, the Power of Attorney recommendation [P20] is stated as prudent but no evidence exists that it was completed, discussed in detail or registered. This is a gap between advice given and action recorded. Third, the cash flow: the Fact Find [P12] shows a monthly deficit of £288, yet the report asserts the client 'are not reliant upon your pension funds' [P14]. The cashflow model [P4] shows pension drawdown is planned from age 69. This is internally inconsistent — if income does not cover expenditure and pension draws are forecast, the client is reliant. Fourth, consolidation as a support need: the Fact Find [P6] records the client 'Wants to consolidate to help him get his head around what he has,' which may signal a comprehension or complexity challenge, but the report does not flag this as a vulnerability or support need; it is treated as an objective. Fifth, the foreseeable harms section [vulnerability/foreseeableHarms[]] lists six harms with mitigations, but does not state how they materially affected the recommendation for this particular client. For a client with zero pension knowledge, market volatility and underperformance risk take on heightened significance, yet the report does not address this explicitly. Sixth, the risk rating upgrade: the questionnaire indicated 4 (Cautious Balanced), the client answered zero for pension knowledge, yet the report (and Risk Profile [P14, P3]) record an upgrade to 5 (Balanced) on the grounds that the questionnaire 'didn't fully reflect your risk appetite' [P14]. The file contains no evidence — such as a detailed discussion record, a comprehension test, or a reassessment of capacity for loss in light of zero pension knowledge — to support why a higher risk rating is appropriate for a novice investor. The check is an overlay on appropriateness: a recommendation appropriate for a resilient, experienced client may not be appropriate for one with zero knowledge and a current cash flow deficit. The report asserts suitability but does not demonstrate that the identified vulnerabilities (knowledge gaps, cash flow strain, need for simplification) were material to shaping the advice. The absence of the canonical path `/vulnerability/perClient[]/impactOnRecommendation[]` is telling: the report identifies harms but does not state their material impact on the recommendation. A Potential Concern arises because: (1) zero pension knowledge is not explicitly linked to the choice of risk rating; (2) foreseeable harms are listed but not tied to material changes in the recommendation; (3) the Power of Attorney recommendation lacks follow-up or evidence of completion; (4) the assertion of non-reliance contradicts the cash flow forecast; and (5) no formal vulnerability assessment appears in the file to show whether the overlay was applied at all.","citations":[{"passageId":"P1","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"Do you understand how stocks and shares work and do you know the risks associated with them? No understanding / knowledge. Do you understand how Enterprise Investment Schemes and Venture Capital Trusts work and do you know the risks associated with them? No understanding / knowledge. Do you understand how pension planning and income in retirement works and do you know the risks associated with them? No understanding / knowledge.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"Have you invested in Unit Trusts and General Investment Accounts within the last 5 years? No. Have you invested in stocks and shares within the last 5 years? No. Have you invested in Enterprise Investment Schemes and Venture Capital Trusts within the last 5 years? No. Have you invested in pension planning and income in retirement products within the last 5 years? No.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P3","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"5 Balanced. As a Balanced investor you do not see yourself as a particularly cautious person and have no strong positive or negative associations with the notion of taking risk. If you have some experience of investments and a degree of understanding of financial matters then you may be suited to a Balanced approach to investing.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P6","source":"Fact Find (Test 1).md","category":"B","quote":"Just needs advice helping him organise his pensions in the best place. Wants to consolidate to help him get his head around what he has.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P12","source":"Fact Find (Test 1).md","category":"B","quote":"Total Net Monthly Income £1,430.00. Total Monthly Expenditure £1,718.00. Total Monthly Disposable Income £-288.00","cells":null},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"You completed an Attitude to Risk questionnaire. We felt that this didn't fully reflect your risk appetite. We agreed that you are a risk rating 5 rather than a 4 as per the questionnaire.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"John, you are aware that investment values can rise as well as fall, and although your experience is limited to your workplace pension arrangements, you understand that returns are not guaranteed. You confirmed that any potential underperformance would not have a detrimental impact on your day-to-day living. You are in receipt of a full State Pension of approximately £230 per week, continue to work as an HGV driver earning around £300 per week net.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"You are happy to proceed with a Risk rating of 5. You confirmed that you wish to increase your Risk rating to 5- Balanced investor, you are aware that this is higher than your agreed risk rating and are happy to take on this risk with your pension. You have confirmed that you are not reliant upon your pension funds and wish for them to have the best growth potential over a 10-year period.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P20","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"It would also be prudent to set up and register Power of Attorney for your financial affairs / health and welfare, to ensure that in the event of your incapacity, your spouse or relative could act on your behalf.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"Your state pension income will cover your bills in retirement. Meaning your pension will be allowed to keep growing for large ad hoc spends.","cells":null}],"severity":"High","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

